[[0,537006,0,7,0,7,"2015-09-24T05:36:57","daskapitalist","",[],"<p>My office is a trifecta of bright white flourescent lights, bright computer monitors, and a glut of windows that combine to give me eyestrain and give my contacts fits from the brightness eight hours a day.</p>\n<p>Voaters, what can I do to help solve this problem without trying to mandate blackout blinds or shutting off half the lights? Are there special sunglasses specific for office workers that might help? Tweaks to make computer monitors less likely to cause eyestrain? Would switching from contacts to glasses help?</p>","How to handle eyestrain from office glare?","","askgoat"],[1,2564186,0,0,0,0,"2015-09-24T10:37:22","drakesdoom","",[],"<p>If you you don't mind looking like your from that 70s show, night driving glasses with full uv protection. </p>"]]
