[[0,537022,0,21,0,21,"2015-09-24T05:41:45","Pwning4Ever","",[],"","Buzzfeed gives disney male characters the \"dadbod\" treatment ","http://www.buzzfeed.com/lorynbrantz/disney-princes-with-average-bodies","fatpeoplehate"],[1,2562564,0,14,0,14,"2015-09-24T06:13:52","Fierce_skinnybitch","",[],"<p>I hate buzzfeed and all their obesity promotion so much. It's ridiculous. </p>"],[1,2562789,0,1,0,1,"2015-09-24T06:35:42","Carsandsarcasm","",[],"<p>Eugh. This is surely a follow-on from the creation of <a href=\"http://www.huffingtonpost.com.au/2015/03/31/disney-princesses-would-look-like-if-they-werent-thin_n_6976336.html?ir=Australia\">Disney princesses if they &quot;weren't thin&quot; (read: were fat)</a>. They are cartoons, for crying out loud. They aren't supposed to be realistic. Appliances also move and talk in these cartoons, but we don't create a fuss about them. Every single thing seems to be too triggering to the lardarses and we have to &quot;correct&quot; it. </p>\n<p>What would happen, too, if the thin people tried to make a big deal over a character being too fat to be realistically healthy? They would be laughed out of the room. </p>"],[1,2562935,0,6,0,6,"2015-09-24T06:53:14","tommychicago","",[],"<p>Yeah because only half the kids today are little fucking porkers, let's encourage the other half to catch up</p>"],[1,2563691,0,10,0,10,"2015-09-24T08:43:46","Nwabudike_Morgan","",[],"<p>You don't put a cuirass on like a shirt, it comes in two pieces, jesus christ.</p>"],[2,2566803,2563691,0,0,0,"2015-09-24T16:38:23","Ser_Alliser_Thorne","",[],"<p>It's Buzzfeed. It's barely a step above tabloids like National Enquirer. </p>"],[2,2568504,2563691,0,0,0,"2015-09-24T18:52:19","BuckinHipster","",[],"<p>What are you talking about I thought you just slid your arms and torso through the hole on that solid, inflexible piece of metal? It's just like a shit, but made of steel or iron, right?</p>"],[3,2569605,2568504,1,0,1,"2015-09-24T20:22:47","32DDbitches","",[],"<blockquo